cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Descriptor-based QSAR models for TBARS/MDA lipid-peroxidation
  inhibition
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite both the accompanying
  article and the original measurement publications listed in
  data/curated_structures_378.csv.
type: software
authors:
  # [AUTHORS: replace with the full author list, in the order used in the
  # article, and add ORCIDs. One entry per author.]
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Hyeon-Cheol
    affiliation: >-
      Forest Biomass Chemistry Laboratory, Department of Environmental
      Materials Science, Gyeongsang National University
license: MIT
license-url: https://github.com/[AUTHORS]/tbars-mda-qsar/blob/main/LICENSE
repository-code: https://github.com/[AUTHORS]/tbars-mda-qsar
keywords:
  - QSAR
  - lipid peroxidation
  - TBARS
  - malondialdehyde
  - molecular descriptors
  - gradient boosting
  - applicability domain
  - antioxidant activity
abstract: >-
  Curated data, fitted model, validation code and every reported table and
  figure for a retrospective QSAR study of TBARS/MDA lipid-peroxidation
  inhibition. A Gradient Boosting regressor on 217 RDKit 2D descriptors was
  fitted to 378 standardized structures compiled from published IC50 values
  and evaluated under a random 80:20 holdout and a scaffold-grouped five-fold
  design, against a training-mean and a 1-NN reference predictor, with a
  distance-based applicability domain and an independent external test set.
